(i) Illustrate Summation, Subtraction, Multiplication and Division Operations on Vectors
Theory

A vector is a one-dimensional data structure that stores elements of the same data type. Arithmetic operations are performed element-wise when vectors have the same length.

Program
# Creating vectors

v1 <- c(10,20,30,40)

v2 <- c(2,4,6,8)

print(v1)

print(v2)

# Addition

add <- v1 + v2

print("Addition")

print(add)

# Subtraction

sub <- v1 - v2

print("Subtraction")

print(sub)

# Multiplication

mul <- v1 * v2

print("Multiplication")

print(mul)

# Division

div <- v1 / v2

print("Division")

print(div)
